note <EdDSA (Ed25519) digital signatures. The clean uniform interface; the per-env native implementation is selected at build time and hidden. Each platform delegates to its built-in Ed25519 (node / browser Web Crypto, rust ed25519-dalek, swift CryptoKit Curve25519, kotlin java.security). Keys and signatures are hex text: the private key and public key are 32 bytes each, a signature is 64 bytes. make-key-pair generates a matched pair together (the only safe way, since a public key cannot be re-derived from a private one on every host). The interface is async to stay uniform with the rest of cryptography.>

load @cluesurf/base/code/native/cryptography/signature
  find make-key-pair-bytes
  find sign-message
  find verify-message

load @cluesurf/base/code/text/string
  find slice

form key-pair
  link private-key, like text
  link public-key, like text

task make-key-pair
  mark async
  like key-pair
  save raw
    call make-key-pair-bytes
      wait true
  send back
    make key-pair
      bind private-key
        call slice
          read raw
          mark 0
          mark 64
      bind public-key
        call slice
          read raw
          mark 64
          mark 128

task sign
  mark async
  take private-key, like text
  take message, like text
  like text
  send back
    call sign-message
      read private-key
      read message
      wait true

task verify
  mark async
  take public-key, like text
  take message, like text
  take signature, like text
  like boolean
  send back
    call verify-message
      read public-key
      read message
      read signature
      wait true
